Cell[TextData[{
 "For a lower risk limit of 0.01%, the limiting function kicks in at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", "=", 
    RowBox[{"11", "%"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "625db2fd-88fe-43cf-8bfe-bbb820f03cf9"],
 ". That seems too high to be useful.\n\nThis is of course a trade-off \
between a sharp knee and a limit that kicks in at a high point. With a soft \
knee, basically all our risk calculations will be affected by the smoothing."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9002973454962273`*^9, 3.9002974202416267`*^9}, {
  3.900297521659307*^9, 3.9002976665421467`*^9}, {3.900298141686062*^9, 
  3.900298147240604*^9}, {3.9002982033773737`*^9, 
  3.900298203377434*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8aa4c944-853f-46b1-ab5e-\
be050ded1205"],

Cell["\<\
What if we try a much lower limit? This would not be something like a limit \
based on max leverage, but rather a sort of \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]absolute \
zero temperature\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] for all risk calculations in the \
system.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.900297771592165*^9, 3.90029787874537*^9}, {
  3.900297923226842*^9, 
  3.900297933715399*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"df39b439-3af4-4f48-bad3-\
828bff647fe6"],

